    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (28 tests, 0 failures/errors, including the 2 new cp17 tests).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `locality` field is a derived, read-only DTO field \u2014 analogous to the existing `displayName`, `initials`, and `membershipTier` \u2014 so I derived it from the persisted `city` at response-mapping time. This covers both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` with no pipeline or entity changes.\n\nTwo edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` property to the `OwnerDto` schema (read-only string) so the generated DTO exposes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` applying the fixed city-to-region table:\n\n   ```\n   Sydney \u2192 NSW, Melbourne \u2192 VIC, Brisbane \u2192 QLD, else UNKNOWN\n   ```\n\nVerified: `Cp17Tests.coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` (Sydney \u2192 `NSW`) and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` (random `Town<seq>` city \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) both pass, and all 28 acceptance tests remain green.",
